## 145. Important Exam Warning

A formula gives the answer only when the diagram satisfies the formula's assumptions.

For example:

```text
\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}6
```

is for a **complete \(n\times n\) square grid**.

If a line is missing:

```text
┌──┬──┐
│  │  │
├──┘  │
│     │
└─────┘
```

the normal grid formula may no longer work.

---

## 146. Deep Concept

Counting figures is essentially a **combinatorial search problem**.

You are searching through:

```text
\text{Vertices}
\rightarrow
\text{Edges}
\rightarrow
\text{Closed paths}
\rightarrow
\text{Valid geometric shapes}
```

Therefore:

```text
\boxed{
\text{Figure Counting}
=
\text{Geometry}
+
\text{Combinatorics}
+
\text{Graph Reasoning}
}
```

---
